.TH AVR\-FIREWALL\-SHOW 1 "" "avr 0.7.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-firewall-show \- Show rules in evaluation order and their source.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr firewall show
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show rules in evaluation order and their source.
.PP
Show rules in evaluation order with repository/organization ownership. Built-in service exceptions are not listed. Running jobs retain their dispatched policy.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository ID or owner/repo. (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output resolved rules as JSON instead of a table.
.SH SEE ALSO
